"42.638606385601584\" cy=\"270.78922726980454\" r=\"4px\" fill=\"currentColor\"></circle><circle cx=\"85.27721277120317\" cy=\"255.25032953960906\" r=\"4px\" fill=\"currentColor\"></circle><circle cx=\"85.27721277120317\" cy=\"239.7114318094136\" r=\"4px\" fill=\"currentColor\"></circle><circle cx=\"106.59651596400396\" cy=\"224.1725340792181\" r=\"4px\" fill=\"currentColor\"></circle><circle cx=\"127.91581915680474\" cy=\"193.0947386188272\" r=\"4px\" fill=\"currentColor\"></circle><circle cx=\"149.23512234960552\" cy=\"162.01694315843622\" r=\"4px\" fill=\"currentColor\"></circle><circle cx=\"191.87372873520712\" cy=\"146.47804542824073\" r=\"4px\" fill=\"currentColor\"></circle><circle cx=\"213.1930319280079\" cy=\"115.40024996784977\" r=\"4px\" fill=\"currentColor\"></circle><circle cx=\"234.5123351208087\" cy=\"68.78355677726337\" r=\"4px\" fill=\"currentColor\"></circle><circle cx=\"255.8316383136095\" cy=\"22.16686358667696\" r=\"4px\" fill=\"currentColor\"></circle></g></svg><div role=\"region\" aria-label=\"Long description for scatterplot\" class=\"sr-only\"><ul><li>The scatterplot has 10 data points.</li><li>The data points are in a linear pattern trending up from left to right.</li><li>The data points have the following coordinates:<ul><li>(12 comma 5)</li><li>(24 comma 10)</li><li>(24 comma 15)</li><li>(30 comma 20)</li><li>(36 comma 30)</li><li>(42 comma 40)</li><li>(54 comma 45)</li><li>(60 comma 55)</li><li>(66 comma 70)</li><li>(72 comma 85)</li></ul></li></ul></div></figure></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">According to the graph, which statement is true?</p>", "keys": ["f1495002-bec4-48d8-9b9b-0de0f6b30802"], "answerOptions": [{"id": "94a5c08c-a371-47c3-8feb-354f1e45cd15", "content": "<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Cutting boards that have a width greater than <math alttext=\"48\"><mn>48</mn>\n</math> centimeters have an average sale price of <math alttext=\"dollar sign 59.00\"><mo>$</mo><mn>59.00</mn></math>.</p>"}, {"id": "d3b420f8-f0d9-41de-a46e-22ecde3725c3", "content": "<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Cutting boards that have a width greater than <math alttext=\"48\"><mn>48</mn>\n</math> centimeters have an average sale price of <math alttext=\"dollar sign 40.00\"><mo>$</mo><mn>40.00</mn></math>.</p>"}, {"id": "0040be54-a139-4ab7-8a7c-bc1278bc6f46", "content": "<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Cutting boards that have a width between <math alttext=\"18\"><mn>18</mn>\n</math> and <math alttext=\"48\"><mn>48</mn>\n</math> centimeters have an average sale price of <math alttext=\"dollar sign 31.20\"><mo>$</mo><mn>31.20</mn></math>.</p>"}, {"id": "f1495002-bec4-48d8-9b9b-0de0f6b30802", "content": "<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Cutting boards that have a width between <math alttext=\"18\"><mn>18</mn>\n</math> and <math alttext=\"48\"><mn>48</mn>\n</math> centimeters have an average sale price of <math alttext=\"dollar sign 23.00\"><mo>$</mo><mn>23.00</mn></math>.</p>"}], "rationale": "<p>Choice D is correct. Each point&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"left parenthesis x comma y right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> on the scatterplot gives the width <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi></math>, in centimeters, and the sale price <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"y\"><mi>y</mi></math>, in dollars, of one of the&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"10\"><mn>10</mn></math> cutting boards put on sale at this store. According to the graph, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"5\"><mn>5</mn></math> cutting boards have widths that are between <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"18\"><mn>18</mn></math> and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"48\"><mn>48</mn></math> centimeters. These widths, in centimeters, are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"24\"><mn>24</mn></math>, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"24\"><mn>24</mn></math>, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"30\"><mn>30</mn></math>, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"36\"><mn>36</mn></math>, and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"42\"><mn>42</mn></math>. The sale prices, in dollars, corresponding to these widths are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"10\"><mn>10</mn></math>, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"15\"><mn>15</mn></math>, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"20\"><mn>20</mn></math>, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"30\"><mn>30</mn></math>, and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"40\"><mn>40</mn></math>, respectively. The average of these sale prices, in dollars, is&nbsp; <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"StartFraction 10 plus 15 plus 20 plus 30 plus 40 Over 5 EndFraction\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>15</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>30</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>40</mn></mrow><mn>5</mn></mfrac></math>, or&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"StartFraction 115 Over 5 EndFraction\"><mfrac><mn>115</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac></math>, which is equivalent to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"23\"><mn>23</mn></math>. Therefore, cutting boards that have a width between&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"18\"><mn>18</mn></math> and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"48\"><mn>48</mn></math> centimeters have an average sale price of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"dollar sign 23.00\"><mo>$</mo><mn>23.00</mn></math>.</p>\n<p>Choice A is incorrect. Cutting boards that have a width greater than <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"48\"><mn>48</mn></math> centimeters have an average sale price of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"dollar sign 63.75\"><mo>$</mo><mn>63.75</mn></math>, not&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"dollar sign 59.00\"><mo>$</mo><mn>59.00</mn></math>.</p>\n<p>Choice B is incorrect. Cutting boards that have a width greater than <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"48\"><mn>48</mn></math> centimeters have an average sale price of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"dollar sign 63.75\"><mo>$</mo><mn>63.75</mn></math>, not&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"dollar sign 40.00\"><mo>$</mo><mn>40.00</mn></math>.</p>\n<p>Choice C is incorrect. Cutting boards that have a width between&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"18\"><mn>18</mn></math> and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"48\"><mn>48</mn></math> centimeters have an average sale price of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"dollar sign 23.00\"><mo>$</mo><mn>23.00</mn></math>, not&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"dollar sign 31.20\"><mo>$</mo><mn>31.20</mn></math>.</p>", "externalid": "3804334d-fce7-4a1c-a320-674b9b7eab71", "correct_answer": ["D"]}